00:16:48.732 --> 00:16:55.598
Dear William, I was happy to receive your letter.

00:16:55.658 --> 00:17:01.866
I went to Angel's mining camp and found Simon Wheeler.

00:17:01.926 --> 00:17:08.920
He told me lots of things about your childhood companion, the Anita's W.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.572
Smiley.

00:17:10.632 --> 00:17:14.393
His first name now is Jim.

00:17:14.454 --> 00:17:20.377
He works as a miner, and he bets on everything that happens at the camp.

00:17:20.436 --> 00:17:24.689
He owns a frog that is a champion jumper.

00:17:24.749 --> 00:17:34.764
He usually wins every bet with his frog, but recently a stranger tricked him, and he lost a $40 bet.

00:17:34.824 --> 00:17:41.539
When you come to California, I'll take you to Angel's Saloon to meet the miners.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:46.492
Your friend, Mark.

00:17:46.552 --> 00:17:52.266
Are you dressed like a gold miner?

00:17:52.326 --> 00:17:57.108
Looking for gold was not easy.

00:17:57.168 --> 00:18:02.438
It was hard work from sunrise to sunset.

00:18:02.498 --> 00:18:06.629
Miners often worked on their knees.

00:18:06.689 --> 00:18:11.340
They needed strong work clothes.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:17.851
Levi Strauss was an immigrant tailor at one of the mining camps.

00:18:17.911 --> 00:18:22.992
He began making work pants called blue jeans.

00:18:23.052 --> 00:18:24.954
or Levi's.

00:18:25.014 --> 00:18:29.978
Blue jeans became very popular in the West.

00:18:30.038 --> 00:18:37.462
Later on, Levi's Strauss opened a blue jeans factory in San Francisco.

00:18:37.522 --> 00:18:48.162
Today, in San Francisco, the Levi's Strauss offices are at Levi's Strauss Plaza by the Bay.

